 * Modular Preprocessing Framework (FGP / LGP / EGP)
 *
 * These modules are designed to be portable, minimal, and domain-agnostic.
 * Users are encouraged to adapt and extend them across a wide range of tasks:
 *
 * - Reinforcement Learning: Use EGP to reshape state distributions via entropy profiling,
 *   improving stability and exploration.
 * - SAT Solving: Apply FGP to suppress repetitive clause patterns, enhancing solver generalization.
 * - Graph Learning: Use LGP to smooth noisy topologies before embedding or classification.
 * - Constraint Programming: Preprocess variable domains to expose tractable regions.
 * - Scheduling & Planning: Use entropy signals to rebalance overloaded constraints.
 * - Bioinformatics: Apply FGP to genomic sequences to highlight structural motifs.
 * - Network Analysis: Use LGP to clarify community structure in noisy graphs.
 * - NLP: Use EGP to normalize token distributions in sparse or imbalanced corpora.
 * - Image Processing: Apply FGP to filter spatial frequency bands before segmentation.
 * - Time Series Forecasting: Use LGP to denoise irregular signals prior to modeling.
 * - Game AI: Use EGP to detect phase transitions in strategic state spaces.
 * - Cybersecurity: Apply entropy-based profiling to detect anomalous patterns.
 *
 * These modules are not complete solutions—they are structural lenses.
 * Customize the signalization, discretization, and semantic guards to fit your domain.
 * Transformation precedes computation: reshape the problem before solving it.
 */



